WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.362
Let’s walk through Present to the room.

00:00:02.362 --> 00:00:06.287
Enter presentation mode deliberately and verify the correct artifact remains

00:00:06.287 --> 00:00:07.650
in context.

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:10.537
Projection removes operator chrome for the room, but it

00:00:10.537 --> 00:00:13.213
does not submit, approve, or change the lifecycle

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:14.812
of the displayed record.

00:00:14.812 --> 00:00:17.050
On this slide, use Present when this screen is

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:18.150
projected.

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:21.350
It hides sidebar chrome, keeps the current slide centered

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:24.900
, and adds the facilitator toolbar for editing, coordination

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:27.413
, engagement, and White Cell forwarding.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:31.960
In practice, enter presentation deliberately, keep sensitive operator

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:34.472
chrome out of view, and exit before returning to

00:00:34.472 --> 00:00:36.035
sidebar navigation.

00:00:36.035 --> 00:00:38.660
Before you continue, verify these points:

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:41.060
Projection does not equal submission.

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:45.023
The presentation toolbar preserves the current artifact context.

00:00:45.023 --> 00:00:48.885
Focus returns to the invoking control when presentation ends.

00:00:48.885 --> 00:00:51.860
When you are ready, use Focus Present control to

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:53.648
move to the live surface.

00:00:53.648 --> 00:00:56.385
The guide will not make the workflow decision for you

00:00:56.385 --> 00:00:56.535
.
